**A coexisting defect is not a cause until you block it and the symptom follows.** On the
reference deploy a real 404 — a missing vendored file — was asserted as the cause of a chart that
would not redraw. Blocking that file on an otherwise-working build did not reproduce the symptom,
which disproved it in one test. Fixing the 404 was still correct on its own merits; it was simply
not this bug. When two candidates appear in the same log, the row is a **control test** — *remove
X, does the symptom appear* — not an observation, and it belongs here for the same reason as §5's
positive control: without it, an empty result and a broken query are the same output.
See OPERATING-THE-PLAN.md §9.

